1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
Why Britain tested nuclear weapons on its own soldiers explained like you are five step one

2
00:00:05,840 --> 00:00:11,640
1952 Britain needs to join the nuclear club America has the bomb the Soviet Union has the bomb

3
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:19,000
Britain wants one they test their first nuclear weapon off the coast of Western Australia Monta Bello Islands October 3rd

4
00:00:19,600 --> 00:00:27,360
1952 it works over the next six years Britain explodes 45 nuclear weapons in Australia in the Pacific in the middle of the ocean

5
00:00:27,360 --> 00:00:33,680
Each test observed by British and Commonwealth servicemen 22,000 of them young men conscripts mostly

6
00:00:33,880 --> 00:00:39,680
Nobody explains what nuclear radiation does to a human body. Nobody explains because nobody wants them to refuse

7
00:00:39,680 --> 00:00:41,560
They are told the tests are safe

8
00:00:41,560 --> 00:00:45,320
They are told to watch some are told to stand up straight and keep their eyes open

9
00:00:45,400 --> 00:00:51,840
So the scientists can measure the psychological effect of a nuclear blast on troops. The troops are the experiment

10
00:00:51,920 --> 00:00:55,320
Nobody tells them that either. Step two Christmas Island

11
00:00:56,200 --> 00:00:58,320
1957 the largest British nuclear test

12
00:00:58,960 --> 00:01:03,160
Operation grapple Ken McGinley is 19 years old a Scottish conscript

13
00:01:03,160 --> 00:01:07,660
He is ordered to sit on the beach facing away from the blast cover your eyes with your hands

14
00:01:07,660 --> 00:01:09,200
He is told when the bomb detonates

15
00:01:09,200 --> 00:01:15,400
He can see the bones in his hands through his closed eyelids through his hands the heat hits him like an oven door opening

16
00:01:15,400 --> 00:01:21,200
Then the shockwave then they are told to turn around and look at a fireball rising over the Pacific no protective clothing

17
00:01:21,200 --> 00:01:24,160
No, dissimeters to measure radiation exposure. No decontamination

18
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:30,200
Afterwards some men are ordered to fly through the mushroom cloud in aircraft to collect air samples

19
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,240
Some are ordered to march into the blast area

20
00:01:32,640 --> 00:01:36,980
Immediately after detonation to test how quickly troops could occupy nuclear territory

21
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:43,520
They marched through ground zero in their uniforms carrying their rifles breathing the air step three the men go home

22
00:01:43,560 --> 00:01:47,720
Get married have children and start getting sick cancer leukemia

23
00:01:48,440 --> 00:01:52,120
Cataracts skin disorders their children born with missing limbs

24
00:01:52,560 --> 00:02:00,320
Chromosomal damage rare cancers their grandchildren affected three generations Ken McGinley son is born without arms. He starts asking questions

25
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:06,080
He finds other veterans asking the same questions. They formed the British nuclear test veterans association

26
00:02:06,080 --> 00:02:08,320
They write to the government the government writes back

27
00:02:08,320 --> 00:02:12,520
There is no evidence of any connection between the tests and your health conditions

28
00:02:12,520 --> 00:02:18,300
They write again same answer every year for decades the same answer. No evidence. No compensation

29
00:02:18,300 --> 00:02:23,080
No acknowledgement the men who stood on Christmas Island Beach are dying taking their evidence with them

30
00:02:23,080 --> 00:02:31,960
The government is waiting step for 2009 the first serious independent study British nuclear test veterans have significantly elevated rates of cancer

31
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:39,440
Leukemia double the rate of comparable men who weren't there the evidence confirmed the government response further review is needed

32
00:02:40,040 --> 00:02:43,280
2012 the Supreme Court rules the veterans can sue for compensation

33
00:02:43,760 --> 00:02:52,640
The government appeals spends millions in legal fees fighting dying men the appeals fail individual cases proceed through the courts one by one

34
00:02:52,640 --> 00:02:56,400
Each veteran must prove their specific cancer was caused by their specific

35
00:02:56,680 --> 00:03:03,600
Test decades after the fact without the dosimetry records the government never kept because they never intended to prove anything

36
00:03:04,000 --> 00:03:07,880
Ken McGinley dies in 2015 still fighting still

37
00:03:08,280 --> 00:03:13,400
Uncompensated today fewer than 2,000 of the original 22,000 are still alive

38
00:03:13,600 --> 00:03:16,880
The government has paid compensation to almost none of them

39
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:20,420
The official position has shifted from denial to acknowledgement

40
00:03:20,420 --> 00:03:27,280
But acknowledgement without compensation is just a different kind of denial Britain built its nuclear deterrent on the bodies of

41
00:03:28,000 --> 00:03:35,000
22,000 young men told them it was safe told them it was their duty then spent 60 years telling them it never happened

42
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:42,400
The bomb worked perfectly the men it was tested on were never supposed to find out and that's just one story inside paladin

43
00:03:42,400 --> 00:03:48,200
It's like Duolingo, but for history lovers download it now and become the most intelligent person in the room

